ning afterwards. Must strain before flow\ncomes. Scanty urine. Acute prostatitis, retention, and\n-feeling of a ball in perineum, {Cann, ind.\\ Fluttering\nin region of kidney. Sugar in urine. [Caps.; GrindcL]\nUnable to urinate without standing with feet wide apart\nand body inclined forward."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"female","label":"Female","startLine":10028,"endLine":10033,"text":"I^bia inflamed, swollen. Pain in vagina.\nHot flashes. Painful tumor of mammee, not ulcerated,\nwith undue secretion of milk. Rapid atrophy of breasts.\nWomen with very large breasts and tumor in the mam-\nmary gland with sharp pain through it."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"male","label":"Male","startLine":10034,"endLine":10037,"text":"Smarting in urethra from neck of bladder to\nmeatus. Gleet. Loss of prostatic fluid. Prostatic en-\nlargement and irritation."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"skin","label":"Skin","startLine":10038,"endLine":10039,"text":"Scrofulous ulcers. Glandular enlargements."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"extremities","label":"Extremities","startLine":10040,"endLine":10041,"text":"Feeling of a band above left knee."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"modalities","label":"Modalities","startLine":10042,"endLine":10044,"text":"IForse, in damp weather; from sitting\non cold stones or pavements ; left side."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"relationship","label":"Relationship","startLine":10045,"endLine":10048,"text":"Compare: Chimaph. maculata (in-\ntense gnawing hunger; burning fever; sensation of\nswelling in arm pits) ; Uva.; Ledum; Epigera."},{"source":"12_boger_synoptic_key","section":"kidneys","label":"Kidneys","startLine":27241,"endLine":27355,"text":"Glands: Liver. Prostate. Mamme (R).\n\nWORSE:\n\nCold damp.\nStanding.\n\nSitting.\n\nBeginning urination.\n\nBETTER:\nWALKING.\n\nROPY or muco-purulent, foul, scanty, thick, turbid, urine. Feels as if sitting on a ball, in the\nperineum; after gonorrhoea. Old nodes in or atrophy of glands. Fluttering in kidney region. Acute\ninflammation in urinary tract. Gravelly urine.\n\nComplementary: Kali-m.\nRelated: Berb. Coc-c. Sabal.\n\nCHINA OFFICINALIS (RUBRA)\n\nREGION:\n\nBLOOD.\n\nCIRCULATION.\n\nSECRETIONS: Digestive. Organs. Liver.\nSpleen.\n\nNerves.\n\nWORSE:\n\nVITAL LOSSES.\n\nTOUCH.\n\nJar.\n\nNoise.\n\nPERIODICALLY: Alternate days (Ars. Nat-m.).\nCold; drafts; wind.\n\nOpen air.\n\nEating; fruit; milk.\n\nMental exertion.\n\nBETTER:\nHard pressure (Lach.).\nLoose clothes.\n\nINTERMITTENCY. PROFUSE, EXHAUSTING DISCHARGES, HAZMORRHAGES, etc.\n(Abro. Calc-hyp. Pho-ac.). Weak, oversensitive and nervous; everything upsets him, light,\nnoise, odors, pain, etc. Hard swelling. Bursting. Rheumatism. Neuralgia. Emaciation. Anzemia.\nDITO OSY,,: scctuvstenmuiene Stubborn. Disobedient. Vertigo; falls backward. Throbbing, bursting,\nswashing, or bruised feeling in brain, < temples. Sore scalp, < touching hair. Hot red ears.\nTinnitus; then vertigo. Deafness. Pale, earthy, sickly look; bluish about eyes. Teeth throb; <\nsucking. Acute, sour or bitter taste, or eructations. Craves delicacies. Quick satiety. Anorexia.\nLoud belching, without relief (Arg-n.). Slow digestion. Sore stomach. Thirst for cold water that\naggravates diarrhoea. Periodical liver symptoms (Quas.). Gall-stones. Swelled liver and spleen.\nFlatulent bloating. Tympanitis. Pain from rectum into genitals. STOOLS; LIENTERIC; dark;\nfoul; watery; BLOODY; painless; < eating; < night. Dark, profuse, clotted menses. Blood\nspitting. Puffing, rattling, breathing. Every motion excites palpitation and takes his breath.\nSuppurative phthisis (Hep.). Painfully sore chest and interscapular spine. Heavy pressure\n(load) on shoulders, between scapulz or on sacrum. Twitching in knees. As ofa band about legs.\nPain in marrow. Drowsy. Heavy, snoring sleep. Anxious dreams. Swelled veins (hands, face).\nMarked prodrome. Clearly staged chill, heat and sweat. Chill, then thirst, then heat, then thirst.\nRed, hot face, with cold hands. Hectic. Sleeplessness, as a prodrome. Thirst during apyrexia.\nDRENCHING SWEATS; AT NIGHT, < least motion; from weakness, etc. Tropical fevers.\nSepsis.\n\nComplementary: Carb-v. Fer. Kali-c.\nRelated: Carb-v.\n\nCHININUM ARSENICICUM\n\nNightsweats; profuse, exhaustive. Oscillating temperature.\n\nCHININUM SULFURICUM\n\nREGION:\nNERVES.\nCIRCULATION.\nDorsal spine.\n\nWORSE:\n\nEXACT PERIODICITY.\nCold, 10-11 A.M.\n\nHead to left.\n\nBETTER:\nYawning.\n\nNeuralgias. .........ccee Sensitive. Nervous. A net, fog or mote before eyes. Tinnitus. Deafness.\nBrow ague. Granular, brickred, urinary sediment. Vertigo, with tinnitus (Sal-ac.). Spine\n(cervico-dorsal) aches, or is tender. Anticipating chills. Delirium during heat. Increasing fever\nand prostration, with profuse nightsweats. Profuse sweat which >, but exhausts. Thirst in all\nstages. Clear apyrexia. Typical malaria. Itching. Petechiz.\n\nRelated: Chin.\n\nCHIONANTHUS VIRGINICA\n\nREGION:\nLIVER."},{"source":"12_boger_synoptic_key","section":"head","label":"Head","startLine":27356,"endLine":27370,"text":"WORSE:\nJarring.\nMotion.\nCold.\n\nBETTER:\nLying on abdomen (Chel.).\n\nBruised soreness; liver, eyeballs, etc. Pains ascend from forehead, stomach, etc. «0.0...\nBilious sick headaches; periodical. Nose, pressure at root or squeezing on bridge (Ham.).\nTongue, greenish-yellow or feels drawn up. Vomiting bitter-sour; hot; bilious; ropy; gushing;\nsetting teeth on edge (Sul-ac.); with colic and cold sweat on forehead and back of hands.\nUneasy ache in liver. Choleo-cystitis. Gall-stones. Griping at navel. As of a band about"},{"source":"12_boger_synoptic_key","section":"abdomen","label":"abdomen","startLine":27371,"endLine":27375,"text":"Weakness in hypogastrium. Stools tarry, clay-colored or undigested. Arrested menses.\nAstringent expectoration. Jaundice. Heat, with aversion to uncover. Cold sweat on back of hands.\n\nRelated: Bry. Iris. Lept. Mere."}],"corpusPassages":[]}